pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*terh₁-","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"τέρετρον","traslitterazione":"téretron","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"testo":"From Old Galician-Portuguese traado (13th century), from Late Latin taratrum (“auger”), attested by Isidore of Seville. Either from Paleo-Hispanic or from Gaulish, from Proto-Celtic *taratrom, from Proto-Indo-European *térh₁-tro-. Alternatively from Ancient Greek τέρετρον (téretron, “borer, gimlet”)"}]}